00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:24.289
A few words about the
abolitionist movement.

00:19:24.289 --> 00:19:26.820
(mumbles) so and I wanna begin

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:29.790
with a quotation from Edward Nathan

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.290
(mumbles) the common struggle.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.900
It is that whatever you
kept alive (indistinct)

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:37.150
the struggle, you will always be

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:39.147
your own (indistinct) equal struggling

00:19:41.447 --> 00:19:43.630
it's equal partners.

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:46.300
Therefore, and this is
one of the problems,

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:47.618
all of the (indistinct).

00:19:47.618 --> 00:19:50.344
If you think of the prison segue

00:19:50.344 --> 00:19:52.850
into (indistinct) of this, you can see

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:55.420
the great purpose of being in that work.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.480
You were constituting them as superior

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:00.735
in the process of trying to right.

00:20:00.735 --> 00:20:02.240
(indistinct) said by saying-

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:03.073
- [Call Operator] This is a call

00:20:03.073 --> 00:20:04.530
