00:20:09.707 --> 00:20:11.511
- [Stevie] You can say (indistinct)

00:20:11.511 --> 00:20:12.344
the abolitionist movement

00:20:12.344 --> 00:20:15.430
has (mumbles indistinctly) of prisoners,

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:18.283
there to be a campaign,
just as a matter of fact.

00:20:19.293 --> 00:20:21.790
It may always be
(indistinct) participation

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:24.320
of prisoners from a
(indistinct) participation

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.187
to acknowledging of equal (indistinct).

00:20:27.473 --> 00:20:30.030
And I find myself repeating this

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:33.533
quite often to people on the outside.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.810
Investigation, they need to look

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:39.763
at the in prison population
and equal partners,

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:43.941
and they need to be
connected to people inside.

00:20:43.941 --> 00:20:45.230
Because the only way they're going know

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:47.509
what's happening in here,

00:20:47.509 --> 00:20:48.826
really what's happening in here

00:20:48.826 --> 00:20:50.954
is that you are connected
to people inside.

00:20:50.954 --> 00:20:52.156
You cannot depend upon on the state

00:20:52.156 --> 00:20:54.619
to tell you how you're treating us.

00:20:54.619 --> 00:20:56.279
You cannot depend up on
the state to tell you

00:20:56.279 --> 00:20:58.130
what's going on in here.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:20:59.750
So, it's important to be connected

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:02.240
to people inside, and
I've also said before

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.950
that if you are doing this work,

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.844
and you are not connected
to someone inside-

00:21:06.844 --> 00:21:08.811
(speaker drowned out by
background noise) wrong.

00:21:08.811 --> 00:21:10.610
So, I think, that's important for us

00:21:10.610 --> 00:21:13.470
to be connected to one another.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:16.070
And that we have to think about ways also

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:18.083
that we can (indistinct) an opportunity

00:21:19.418 --> 00:21:20.251
to contribute for people inside

00:21:20.251 --> 00:21:21.084
and how we can get...

00:21:21.084 --> 00:21:22.930
How we can actually grow

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:24.530
the capacity people inside.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:26.830
And one of the ways is collaboration.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:28.701
I encourage everyone

00:21:28.701 --> 00:21:32.436
to truly collaborate with people inside,

00:21:32.436 --> 00:21:33.457
to (indistinct) the capacity

00:21:33.457 --> 00:21:35.243
of the people inside.

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:37.480
Which is really important instead

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:42.119
of coming to the project
already formulated

00:21:42.119 --> 00:21:44.812
and asking people to participate in it,

00:21:44.812 --> 00:21:47.470
and asking you to actually create

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:49.674
these programs, create these projects

00:21:49.674 --> 00:21:51.540
for the people inside, and not be like

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:54.090
the DOC, Department of Corrections,

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:56.290
where actually, they never
asked for our consent.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.290
And they only asked for our cooperation,

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.260
actually kinda forced us to cooperate.

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:03.350
That's kinda, a lot of people out there

00:22:03.350 --> 00:22:04.783
who are doing this work too.

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:06.850
And I mention consent,

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:10.969
'cause quite often, people outside

00:22:10.969 --> 00:22:13.837
who are doing this work,
they make statements.

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:17.610
They (indistinct) campaign,

00:22:17.610 --> 00:22:21.023
they take action on
behalf of people inside,

00:22:22.090 --> 00:22:25.553
but they don't ask us
if that's what we want.

00:22:25.553 --> 00:22:27.400
They don't ask our opinion.

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:28.601
They don't ask us for our consent-

00:22:28.601 --> 00:22:29.434
- [Call Operator] This is a call

00:22:29.434 --> 00:22:30.540
from Pennsylvania State

00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:33.230
Correctional Institution, Camp Hill.

